    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, my tomato plants are acting weird. the leaves at the bottom are turning yellow but the ones at the top look okay. what do you think is going on and how can i fix the soil?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing lower leaves while the top stays green is a classic sign of nitrogen deficiency, since the plant moves available nitrogen to new growth first. It can also indicate overwatering or poor drainage, which stresses roots and blocks nutrient uptake.\n\nFor the soil, work in some compost or a balanced fertilizer (like 10-10-10), and if you suspect overwatering, let the top inch of soil dry out between waterings. Also check that your plants have good drainage—if they're in containers, make sure there are holes at the bottom.",
      "source": "target",
